  "cards": [
    { "dot": "emerald", "title": "How the capabilities fit together", "items": [
      "Each capability (metamodels, validation, models, grammars, transformations, events/gamification, integrations, recovery, publication) is an independent backend service, called directly by the workbench",
      "All of them share the same canonical JSON document store; there is no central database and no direct coupling between sibling capabilities",
      "Integrations and external recovery are the only doors out of the local process: third-party transformation engines and remote repositories"
    ]},
    { "dot": "cyan", "title": "The lifecycle of a typical capability", "items": [
      "The workbench calls its capability service through that service's own REST resource",
      "The service validates the request and applies its domain logic (e.g. compiling a grammar, running a transformation)",
      "The result is stored in the shared canonical persistence and, where relevant, recorded in the audit log",
      "An operation that needs to run something outside the process (an external engine, a remote repository) first goes through the sandboxed process launcher"
    ]},
    { "dot": "rose", "title": "What the security layer guarantees", "items": [
      "Every incoming request passes through shape/size hardening before reaching any capability",
      "Every external process (recovery, integration, native transformation, packaging) runs sandboxed, with a minimal environment and bounded output",
      "A missing third-party MDE engine fails closed; its behavior is never simulated"
    ]},
    { "dot": "slate", "title": "Relationship to the other views", "items": [
      "This view explains the HOW (subsystem responsibilities and interactions); it cites no files or code lines — that lives in hydra-architecture.en.html",
      "The user view (hydra-user-overview.en.html) explains the WHAT, in non-technical language",
      "All three views share the same canonical component IDs (for example b_transformation) for the capabilities that appear in more than one"
    ]}
